{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md | sed -n '55,85p'\"","aggregated_output":"    55\t**`(vm :type)` offers four evaluators; the default is `:semantic`.**\n    56\tThe shell supports `:ast-walker` (the tree walker), `:semantic` (the linear\n    57\tsemantic VM), `:stack` (the de Bruijn stack kernel), and `:register` (the de\n    58\tBruijn register kernel). `:semantic` is the default when no `:vm-type` is\n    59\tgiven. Asking for any other type is an error naming what is supported.\n    60\tSwitching rebuilds the session and clears the value history.\n    61\t\n    62\tWhichever VM runs, the shell never reads a value from the VM record: a\n    63\thalted evaluation's value is appended to the output `dao.stream` medium as\n    64\ta `:repl/result` token, after the round's prints, and the shell reads it\n    65\tfrom there exactly as it reads printed output.\n    66\t\n    67\t**There is no `(telemetry)` command.** Telemetry is not part of the v2 slice\n    68\tin any form. `(telemetry)` is answered with a message naming the v1 REPL, and\n    69\t`--telemetry` / `--telemetry-stream` are rejected rather than ignored. There\n    70\tis no `ws://` telemetry sink.\n    71\t\n    72\t**Evaluation runs on session-owned v2 program media.** The REPL session\n    73\t(`make-session`), not any one VM, owns the program media for all four VMs.\n    74\tEvery program, including a datom program typed at the prompt, is appended\n    75\tto the session's ingress ring buffer (declared capacity 4096); the expander\n    76\tforwards it to the session's program medium, from which the selected VM\n    77\tingests it between batches. A gap (batches evicted before the VM saw them)\n    78\tis fatal to the current evaluation:\n    79\tthe loss is reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`,\n    80\trather than resuming as if execution were complete.\n    81\t\n    82\t**The evaluator is step-driven everywhere.** One `repl-step` owns all REPL and\n    83\tRPC state on every host; input adapters only append lines to the composition's\n    84\tinput medium. A remote evaluation returns immediately with a request id, and\n    85\tthe result prints when it completes. Input typed while a request is\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
