src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-258-   requires -- no receive path exists in this phase, but this function's\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-259-   own shape (bytes in, hash out, no host-value peeking) already supports\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-260-   that later use.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-261-  [register-image]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-262-  (jing/sha256 (str descriptor-hash (encode-register-image register-image))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-263-\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-264-\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-265-;; =============================================================================\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-266-;; body-liveness (design section 4.5)\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:533:(defn image-hash\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-534-  \"The ONE function that computes H (S2 item 6): `jing/sha256` over the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-535-   descriptor hash (which already folds in the lowering-contract\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-536-   version) concatenated with the canonical instruction vector's own\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-537-   bytes -- pc-indexed tuples, refs already resolved to pcs, no header,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-538-   exact scalar bytes. `jing/sha256`, not `jing/sha256-bytes`: this\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-539-   dimension's canonical encoding is hex text (`encode-image` returns a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-540-   string, via `framed`/`to-hex`), the same shape `jing/sha256` hashes\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-541-   for `yin.vm.debruijn/dimension-hash`, so hashing the string directly\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-542-   is the fit; `sha256-bytes` would apply to a raw byte buffer this\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-543-   encoder never produces. H is the ONLY executable and sharing identity\nsrc/cljc/